  "verbalization": "Sisomicin appears to interact with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex through a shared target, Integrin beta-6, which is targeted by multiple compounds, including Sisomicin, Lonijaposide T, and Clinopodic Acid A. This suggests that Sisomicin may exert its effects by modulating the activity of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, potentially through the regulation of Integrin beta-6. The presence of multiple compounds targeting the same downstream pathway implies a possible mechanism of action involving the interaction with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, possibly through the modulation of gene expression or chromatin modification. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Sisomicin to influence cellular processes mediated by the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
